// It does NOT trust that re-sync: every text file it edits is rebuilt from origin's blob + its rows, and every frame's original is checked
// on origin (THE BASE IS ORIGIN'S BLOB, the boss-feet-calib rule).
// Per user: "Yes go ahead" - upscale the soft / stretched boss and monster art for FREE with the local Real-ESRGAN, previews first.
//   ART - 444 files REPLACED under their own names:
//     KEEP (drawn bigger than their art; stored at 1.6-2x): the Tower Sovereign's volley / drain / swing / pillar (x1.667), Aetherion
//       form 1 idle + attack (x1.6), Legosaurus idle / walk / attack / charge + his two stills (x1.75), the Tower Arbiter's swing / pillar /
//       verdict (x1.6), Path's Bane's swing (x2). Pipeline: deblock (bilateral), Real-ESRGAN x4plus-anime x4 (local GPU, no credits), ONE
//       lanczos3 reduction onto the new canvas, light luminance unsharp (sigma 1, amount 0.5), a shadow guard (dark areas keep their
//       local level: the model crushes near-black to 0), a range clamp (no new rim / sliver brighter or darker than the art's own local
//       range +-12) and the alpha edge band faded back to the art (alpha 150-250); alpha = origin's resampled onto the new canvas. Sets
//       drawn from a cut canvas are cut HORIZONTALLY only (their ink + >= 24 px; the width makes the drawn width an exact even number),
//       never vertically (a hit region is a fraction of the drawn height). WebP q94 + lossless alpha.
//     SAME SIZE (soft at their own size): the Sovereign's lunge / collapse / strike, Gravitos form 2 soul + supernova, form 1 slam /
//       punch / soul / beam - the same pipeline onto the unchanged canvas, alpha byte for byte.
//     RECIPE (the Arbiter's v0.30.1815 free sharpen: ink flatten, lanczos x2, luminance shock filter 6 it / sigma 2 / th 0.4, bright
//       sliver limiter, lanczos back, glow-safe blend by the original alpha, per-channel gain): Mira Fallen (5 sets), Aetherion form 2
//       (6 sets), Gravitos form 2 beam / punch / slam / walk, King Krook (4 sets) - alpha byte for byte, WebP q90.
//   TABLES that describe those pixels, each value from its own generator on a mirror holding the new frames (data/sprite_bbox.js,
//     sprite_edges.js, anim_calib_manifest.js + its stamp, boss_resize_manifest.js), and sw.js CACHE +1 (art replaced under its names).
//   CALIBRATION - data/anim_calib.js through scripts/apply_anim_patch.mjs (LX_ANIM_PATCH:1): each KEEP set's s / dx / dy re-solved so
//     every frame draws where and as big as before at both facings (measured in the game: <= 0.5 px); its drawn height x s is the
//     origin's, so every hit region (a fraction of it) is the same box in the world. Timings and hit boxes untouched.
//   TEST PINS - the suites that pin the old canvases / calibration rows (see PINS).
// GUARDED: each replaced frame must hold EITHER origin's bytes OR the new ones; each table value EITHER the old OR the new value; each
// calibrated state EITHER the old OR the new s/dx/dy; each test pin EITHER its old OR its new text - anything else aborts before writing.
